=== lsof ===
DESCRIPTION ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
lsof: -e not followed by a file system path: "lp" lsof 4.95.0 Defaults in
parentheses; comma-separated set (s) items; dash-separated ranges.


FLAGS (43) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-?      list help
 or -h
-a      AND selections (OR)
-b      avoid kernel blocks
-c c    cmd c ^c /c/[bix]
+c w    COMMAND width (9)
+d s    dir s files
-d s    select by FD set
+D D    dir D tree *SLOW?*
-e s    exempt s *RISKY*
 or +e
-i      select IPv[46] files
-K [i]  list|(i)gn tasKs
-l      list UID numbers
-n      no host names
-N      select NFS files
-o      list file offset
-O      no overhead *RISKY*
-P      no port names
-Q      allow failed search
-R      list paRent PID
-s      list file size
-t      terse listing
-T      disable TCP/TPI info
-U      select Unix socket
-v      list version info
-V      verbose search
-w      Warnings (+)
 or +w
-X      skip TCP&UDP* files
-Z Z    context [Z]
--      end option scan
-E      display endpoint info
+E      display endpoint info and files
-f      +filesystem or -file names
 or +f
-f[gG]  flaGs
 or +f
-F [f]
-L [l]  list (+) suppress (-) link counts < l (0 = all; default = 0)
 or +L
+m[m]   use|create mount supplement
-M      portMap registration (-)
 or +M
-o o    o 0t offset digits (8)
-p s    exclude(^)|select PIDs
-S [t]  t second stat timeout (15)
-T fqs  TCP/TPI Fl,Q,St (s) info
-g [s]  exclude(^)|select and print process group IDs
-i i    select by IPv[46] address:
        [46][proto][@host|addr][:svc_list|port_list]
